# Firebase (PRD §4.1) is @react-native-firebase/*: the native SDKs read
# credential FILES, not env vars. There are no EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* values.
#
#   Android   apps/mobile/google-services.json
#   iOS       apps/mobile/GoogleService-Info.plist
#
# Both are git-ignored (PRD §16). Download them from the Firebase console
# (Project settings -> Your apps) and drop them next to app.config.ts for a
# local build. For EAS builds, upload each ONCE as a file-type environment
# variable per environment (development / preview / production), which
# eas.json maps to each build profile:
#
#   eas env:create --scope project --environment preview \
#       --name GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON --type file --value ./google-services.json
#   eas env:create --scope project --environment preview \
#       --name GOOGLE_SERVICES_PLIST --type file --value ./GoogleService-Info.plist
#
# EAS exposes each as an absolute path in the env var of the same name;
# app.config.ts reads them. With neither file present the app still builds and
# boots into the §12.4 offline path (Home: "Firebase: not configured").
